  "content": {
    "id": "p23-review-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Solve each equation for $0^{\\circ}\\le\\theta\\le360^{\\circ}$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p23-review-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$2\\cos\\theta-1=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=60^{\\circ},\\ 300^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2\\cos\\theta&=1\\\\\\cos\\theta&=\\frac12\\end{align*}$$\nThe related angle is $60^{\\circ}$. Cosine is positive in quadrants I and IV.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=60^{\\circ}\\text{ or }360^{\\circ}-60^{\\circ}\\\\\\theta&=60^{\\circ}\\text{ or }300^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-review-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$2\\cos\\theta+1=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=120^{\\circ},\\ 240^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2\\cos\\theta&=-1\\\\\\cos\\theta&=-\\frac12\\end{align*}$$\nThe related angle is $60^{\\circ}$. Cosine is negative in quadrants II and III.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=180^{\\circ}-60^{\\circ}\\text{ or }180^{\\circ}+60^{\\circ}\\\\\\theta&=120^{\\circ}\\text{ or }240^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-review-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$2\\sin\\theta-\\sqrt3=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=60^{\\circ},\\ 120^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2\\sin\\theta&=\\sqrt3\\\\\\sin\\theta&=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nThe related angle is $60^{\\circ}$. Sine is positive in quadrants I and II.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=60^{\\circ}\\text{ or }180^{\\circ}-60^{\\circ}\\\\\\theta&=60^{\\circ}\\text{ or }120^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-review-q9-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$2\\sin\\theta+\\sqrt3=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=240^{\\circ},\\ 300^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2\\sin\\theta&=-\\sqrt3\\\\\\sin\\theta&=-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nThe related angle is $60^{\\circ}$. Sine is negative in quadrants III and IV.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=180^{\\circ}+60^{\\circ}\\text{ or }360^{\\circ}-60^{\\circ}\\\\\\theta&=240^{\\circ}\\text{ or }300^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-review-q9-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$5\\sin\\theta+5=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=270^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}5\\sin\\theta&=-5\\\\\\sin\\theta&=-1\\end{align*}$$\nOn the unit circle, the $y$-coordinate is $-1$ only at $270^{\\circ}$ in the given interval.\n$$\\theta=270^{\\circ}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-review-q9-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$4\\cos\\theta-4=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=0^{\\circ},\\ 360^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}4\\cos\\theta&=4\\\\\\cos\\theta&=1\\end{align*}$$\nOn the unit circle, the $x$-coordinate is $1$ at $0^{\\circ}$ and $360^{\\circ}$. Both endpoints are included.\n$$\\theta=0^{\\circ}\\text{ or }360^{\\circ}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
